==English==

===Etymology 1===
There was a Frankish ninth century St. Ava (of the Germanic root ''avi'', related to [[Evelyn]]), but the English Ava seems to date from the nineteenth century as a variant of [[Eva]]. It has also been used as an anglicization of {{noncog|ga|Aoife|lit=beautiful}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪvə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪvə}}

